{
  "lesson_id": "c1_subject_verb_agreement_advanced_rules",
  "level": "C1",
  "title": "Subject–verb agreement: Advanced rules",
  "description": "Subject–verb agreement становится сложнее, когда subject separated from verb, содержит quantifiers или является collective noun/amount expression.",
  "theory": {
    "rule_id": "RULE-C1-10-RU",
    "lesson_num": 10,
    "title": "Правила: Subject–verb agreement: Advanced rules",
    "level": "C1",
    "overview": "Subject–verb agreement становится сложнее, когда subject separated from verb, содержит quantifiers или является collective noun/amount expression.",
    "main_rule": "Verb agrees with grammatical subject, not the nearest noun. Each/every/everyone take singular verb. Collective nouns can vary by variety and meaning. Amounts/periods can take singular when seen as one unit. Titles usually singular.",
    "form": "singular subject + singular verb. plural subject + plural verb.",
    "when_why": "The list of required documents is on the website. / Each employee is responsible. / Everyone has received the message. / Ten minutes is enough. / Five years is a long time.",
    "examples": "The list of required documents is on the website. → Список необходимых документов находится на сайте.\nEach employee is responsible for the result. → Каждый сотрудник отвечает за результат.\nEveryone has received the message. → Все получили сообщение.\nTen minutes is enough. → Десяти минут достаточно.\n“Great Expectations” is a novel. → «Большие надежды» — роман.",
    "special_cases": "Collective nouns can vary: The team is working... / In some British contexts, the team are discussing... Meaning and variety matter.",
    "common_mistakes": "❌ The list of changes are ready. → ✅ The list of changes is ready.\n❌ The nearest noun controls the verb. → ✅ Согласование определяется настоящим подлежащим.",
    "dont_confuse": "Не смотри на nearest noun. Найди real grammatical subject.",
    "quick_summary": "Subject controls agreement.\nDon't be distracted by intervening nouns.\neach/every/everyone → singular.\nAmounts/titles can be singular as units."
  },
